      "severity": "High",
      "file": "CaseHistoryController.cls",
      "lines": "1",
      "explanation": "The class is declared 'without sharing', which means record-level sharing is ignored. The @AuraEnabled method can be called from Lightning components and will return all Cases regardless of the user's sharing permissions. An authenticated user could access Cases they should not have access to based on record ownership or sharing rules.",
      "remediation": "Change the class declaration from 'public without sharing' to 'public with sharing' to enforce record-level sharing, or use 'WITH USER_MODE' in the SOQL query to enforce both object/field permissions and sharing rules."
    }
  ]
}
